{"title":"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 25</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following sets of whole numbers has the largest average?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/a/77a4eba7283d0a8b0d0e6ac3a0c1716407b0fee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\text{multiples of 2 between 1 and 101} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\text{multiples of 3 between 1 and 101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"572\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/455ef1fa4c6ae1b4261b5833901a59b6840daa17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(C)}\\ \\text{multiples of 4 between 1 and 101} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\text{multiples of 5 between 1 and 101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"573\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906906c61828ae8186b9050881d498b165e05b52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(E)}\\ \\text{multiples of 6 between 1 and 101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"268\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the average of the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.  There must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/5/9b5b3ebaa62b7e94ed598e4ac145fe7a44040873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{101}{n} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"54\" height=\"45\" /> (the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2743f46c9804eaf4e7f33c6ba6fbadeb957e495c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{101}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />) multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283e1ae3a345290f253fc4acf944c16383655273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(n) = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{101}{n} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"112\" height=\"45\" />.  Then the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/96880fb2db4afcf70a7050628be0c522de91dbac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{n, 2n, ..., g(n) \\cdot n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />, so their average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c786e1dba5f5475f57bcaf23273ae05dd7cef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=\\frac{n + 2n + ... + g(n) \\cdot n}{g(n)} = \\frac{n}{g(n)} (1 + 2 + ... + g(n)) = \\frac{n}{g(n)} \\cdot \\frac{g(n)(g(n)+1)}{2} = \\frac{n(g(n)+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"761\" height=\"45\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/56050a188ba5dc3affba01587ee1bec8d8cd43f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) = 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb73725eccc80d09b0e9fd350ac549b3d239ab8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3) = 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/7/7c7fc1f3eab070146217dd715c553e628e734ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4) = 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c836a0e98d354694568122b76c0aa5e51833ca85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(5) = 52.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/1/fd10af54dd27222019e06390b1e43ce599d51361.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(6) = 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, thus the set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f23b8eb2261b0ed525caf38771098515275fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{multiples of 5 between 1 and 101}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"288\" height=\"30\" /> has the greatest average.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The elements of each answer choice form arithmetic sequence. Since the sum of any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-term arithmetic sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee0fe5389f25ab5b4818b90781b0d00114eb1a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_1, ..., a_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22f00834844ceeca6d46ed43192d1b4ba6697604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{2}(a_1+a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"34\" />, its average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/126753a04bbb3f71cd2481e516b4e38e7430afa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(a_1+a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />, that is, the average of its first and last terms.  Therefore, the averages of (A), (B), (C), (D), and (E) are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3e504c4afe2a7960aa28eb82a50489102b8bf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(2+100) = 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29ecc7e699d54569c6e2a29c4ee9da2365782be4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(3+99) = 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c61ef772a5b3bc6a6c5ac157a01522893d0ba6db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(4+100) = 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b204c41532c9267fe5bd9279a1addcbb29d9e7a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(5+100) = 52.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b23e7ed1fa7bd8ae75c701dc7fe211ffae48ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(6+96) = 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" />, respectively. So of these, the set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f23b8eb2261b0ed525caf38771098515275fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{multiples of 5 between 1 and 101}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"288\" height=\"30\" /> has the largest average.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/eRh_yzMOD14\">https://youtu.be/eRh_yzMOD14</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME\" title=\"1986 AJHSME\">1986 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a